# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS REPO IS THE PUBLIC SITE. GitHub Pages serves the repo ROOT — the
# files listed below are the ones students load, and everything tracked
# here is world-readable at a stable URL. There is no mirror and no publish
# step: editing a file listed below edits the live site. (If a
# `github_pages/` folder is still on disk, it is a stale second clone of
# this repo, not a deploy target — see _archive/README.md.)
#
# Allow-list deploy. NOTHING in this folder is published unless it is
# explicitly listed below. So any PDFs, reports, notes, or scratch files
# you keep here stay on your computer — even ones you add later.
#
# To publish a new top-level file/folder, add another "!/name" line.
#
# THIS IS A MULTI-STUDENT APP. It lives in a folder named after one
# student, and that is an accident of history, not a scope. Several
# students use it, more will, and each one accumulates tutor-facing
# material — a ledger, a shortlist, a report, class notes. Section 5 is
# what keeps that material out of the public site NO MATTER WHERE IT IS
# PUT. Read it before adding a file about a student anywhere in this tree.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) Ignore everything at the project root by default
/*

# 2) ...then publish ONLY the web app:
!/.gitignore
!/.nojekyll
!/index.html
!/progress.html
!/exam.html
!/custom.html
!/review.html
!/README.md
!/shared/
!/Linear_Equations_App/
!/Linear_Functions_App/
!/Nonlinear_Functions_App/
!/Systems_and_Expressions_App_v2/
!/Proportionality_App/
!/Statistical_Reasoning_App/
!/Core_Geometry_App/
!/Analytical_Geometry_App/
!/Data_Analysis_Probability_App/
!/Challenge_App/

# 3) Tutor-side tooling. TRACKED, deliberately, so it survives a fresh clone —
#    the question banks cannot be rebuilt without it. It is served by Pages like
#    everything else, so it must stay free of passwords and student data: these
#    hold no credentials, and a student's roster key is just their display name.
!/build_challenge_set.py
!/CHALLENGE_SETS_RUNBOOK.md
#    The payload builders that generate each app's data/questions.js:
!/build_analytical_geometry_payload.py
!/build_core_geometry_payload.py
!/build_data_app_payload.py
!/build_linear_app_payload.py
!/build_nonlinear_app_payload.py
!/build_proportionality_payload.py
!/build_stats_payload.py
!/build_systems_app_payload.py
#    Bank sanity checker (duplicate ids, missing answer keys, thin pools):
!/audit-question-pools.js
#    The Google Apps Script behind the tutor Sheet. It used to live ONLY in
#    Google, unversioned, which is exactly how it drifted out of step with the
#    sheet's own columns and silently stopped recording student names. This
#    folder is now the source of truth; the copy in Google is a deployment of
#    it. It carries no credentials (SHARED_KEY is already public in session.js).
!/tools/

# 3b) The archive. PUBLISH WHAT WORKS — so the retired CODE in _archive/ is
#     deliberately NOT published: it is superseded or broken, and the live site
#     should not serve it. It stays on disk, out of the way.
#
#     Its README is the exception, and is tracked on purpose: it is the RECORD —
#     what was retired, why, and which mistakes not to repeat (do not fork the
#     Challenge module per student; do not trust github_pages/). A lesson nobody
#     can read after a fresh clone is not a lesson.
!/_archive/
_archive/*
!/_archive/README.md

# 4) The test toolchain. The APP has no dependencies and no build step — this is
#    only so `npm install && npm test` works on a fresh clone, which is what the
#    jsdom harness in shared/*.test.js needs. node_modules/ stays ignored by the
#    rule above; the lockfile is deliberately not tracked (dev-only, and this is a
#    public site — there is no point publishing an npm dependency tree).
!/package.json

# OS cruft, even inside published folders
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/

# ⚠ github_pages/ — NOT a mirror. It is a SECOND CLONE of this repository, on
# main, 27 commits behind and diverged, with push enabled to the real remote.
# A commit+push from inside it would clobber months of work on main; the root
# CLAUDE.md records that a stale mirror has corrupted this repo once already.
# It holds no unique history (all 27 commits verified present in this repo) and
# its files duplicate the tracked root, so it is safe to delete — see
# _archive/README.md. Ignored explicitly, belt and braces, so it can never be
# committed while it is still sitting there.
/github_pages/

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5) TUTOR-FACING MATERIAL — never tracked, at ANY depth.
#
# Rules 1–4 are an allow-list, and an allow-list only guards the ROOT. Put a
# LEDGER.md inside shared/ or any *_App/ — a folder that is already published —
# and it ships to the public site. That hole was open: `shared/LEDGER.md`,
# `Linear_Equations_App/LEDGER.md` and `Challenge_App/notes.md` were all
# publishable. These patterns close it wherever the file lands.
#
# This matters more as the roster grows. Root rule 6 of the house rules: never
# write an assessment of a student into a file the student can read — and every
# file below is world-readable the moment it is tracked. A ledger says what a
# named minor cannot do yet. A shortlist is a list of what they keep getting
# wrong. Neither belongs at a public URL.
#
# These are DENY rules placed last, so they beat every "!" above. If you ever
# need one of these published, do not delete the pattern — that silently opens
# it for every student. Add a single targeted "!" line and say why.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Per-student ledgers — the tutor's record of what is taught, shaky, and due.
LEDGER.md
*LEDGER.md
*ledger.md

# Challenge shortlists — literally "what this named student keeps missing".
challenge_shortlist_*.md

# Class notes, session plans, and performance reports, wherever they are kept.
Class Summaries/
*Session_Plan*.html
*Performance Report*
*performance_report*

# A general escape hatch: name anything tutor-only with this suffix and it can
# never be published by accident, wherever you put it.
*.tutor.md
*.tutor.json

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHAT IS ACTUALLY PUBLISHED
#
# Tracked here = world-readable. Never allow-list a file holding a password or
# a key.
#
# The tutor tooling in rule 3 IS published, deliberately and by decision
# (19 Jul 2026): it is tracked so it survives a fresh clone, because the nine
# question banks cannot be rebuilt without it. An earlier version of this note
# claimed it "stays local" — that was simply false, and false in the reassuring
# direction, which is the worst kind.
#
# What that costs: the builders carry roster keys and display names, so the
# tooling names students on the public site. That is accepted. What it must
# never carry is a password, a key, or anything ABOUT a student's ability —
# section 5 covers the latter wherever it is written.
#
# Passwords: gate.js holds SHA-256 hashes, never plaintext. Accepted as fine —
# it is a soft gate, not security, and it is documented as such in AGENTS.md.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
